---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StatusGovernance from "../components/StatusGovernance.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Unity House Pilot" description="The council-awarded Unity House pilot from Visio Nova Mundi CIC: six bilingual community health and wellbeing sessions in South Waltham Forest within the September 2026–March 2027 grant period.">
  <section class="heroBlock">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Council-awarded pilot · September 2026–March 2027</p>
      <h1>Romanian Healthy Living &amp; Community Kitchen Pilot</h1>
      <p class="lead">A six-session Unity House pilot for adults in South Waltham Forest, supporting practical low-cost nutrition, healthy meal preparation, physical activity, local connection and sustainable living.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/timeline">View the timeline</a><a class="btn" href="#community-engagement">Get involved locally</a></div>
    </div>
    <aside class="statusCard vnm-glass-card"><p class="statusLabel">Current status</p><h2>Awarded pilot in delivery window</h2><p>VNM has been awarded funding under the London Borough of Waltham Forest Community Health Champions Microgrant Fund for a six-session pilot.</p><span class="statusPill">Sep 2026–Mar 2027 · six sessions</span></aside>
  </section>

  <StatusGovernance stage="Awarded / funded pilot · current delivery window" operator="Visio Nova Mundi CIC — CIC-led programme" delivery="Six hosted community health and wellbeing sessions for adults in South Waltham Forest, within September 2026–March 2027. This is the awarded scope, not a statement that all sessions have taken place." partnership="Award under the London Borough of Waltham Forest Community Health Champions Microgrant Fund; no broader institutional partnership is implied." funding="Awarded for the six-session pilot." boundary="Phase 1 uses agreed host-venue arrangements. The award does not establish a permanent centre, public waste-collection service or active food-surplus operation." />

  <section class="section communityUpdate">
    <p class="eyebrow">Current delivery / funded pilot</p><h2>Hosted sessions, existing community venues</h2>
    <p>Individual session dates and the venue remain subject to confirmation, within the awarded September 2026–March 2027 delivery window.</p>
    <p>Phase 1 food activity is delivered only within the agreed host-venue arrangements and applicable food-safety responsibilities. Any extension beyond the funded session scope would require separate review of operator responsibilities, food-safety controls and required approvals.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section modelIntro">
    <div class="sectionHead">
      <p class="eyebrow">Long-term concept study</p>
      <p><strong>Long-term conceptual study. Phase 1 is delivered as a hosted programme using existing community venues.</strong></p>
      <h2>A community house that turns local resources into community value</h2>
      <p>The longer-term vision is a neighbourhood circular-economy hub: a trusted place where suitable local surplus, reusable materials and appropriate waste streams can be brought together and managed responsibly.</p>
      <p>The six funded sessions are the first controlled, real-world validation phase for the wider Unity House model. They will generate learning about community health, food, reuse and connection; that evidence can guide the next steps toward a permanent neighbourhood hub and a scalable network.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="modelGrid">
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Safe edible surplus</h3><p>Where food is legally sourced and safe to use, suitable edible surplus could help create affordable meals and shared learning.</p></article>
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Reuse, repair and upcycling</h3><p>Reusable materials could be sorted into repair, upcycling, sharing or other routes that keep useful resources in community use.</p></article>
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Appropriate treatment</h3><p>Unavoidable food waste could go to appropriate composting or other authorised treatment through competent partners.</p></article>
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Jobs, learning and belonging</h3><p>The wider model aims to create local jobs and training, support volunteering and help neighbours from different communities meet and work together.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="safeguard"><strong>Statutory boundary:</strong> Any future collection, storage, transport, preparation, redistribution or treatment would need separate scope, responsible partners and the relevant food-safety, waste, environmental-permitting, planning, insurance, safeguarding and data-protection controls.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section communityUpdate" id="community-engagement">
    <p class="eyebrow">Funded pilot · South Waltham Forest</p>
    <h2>Six sessions to learn what is useful, safe and worth continuing</h2>
    <p>The funded programme is a free, community-based health and wellbeing pilot for adults in South Waltham Forest, with Romanian-English access and an open invitation to learn from local residents and other communities.</p>
    <p>The pilot focuses on practical low-cost nutrition, healthy meal preparation, physical activity, connection to local support, food-waste and reuse learning, and opportunities for neighbours to meet. It is health promotion and signposting—not clinical advice, diagnosis or treatment.</p>
    <p>We are also looking for <strong>Romanian-speaking and Romanian-English volunteers and community connectors</strong> who would like to help us reach residents, support communication and gather community feedback.</p>
    <div class="volunteerRow">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Interested in helping?</p>
        <p class="volunteerBoundary">Volunteers may support Romanian-English communication, community introductions, welcoming residents, approved outreach, simple feedback collection and identifying practical needs and barriers. This is a community-support role, not a clinical or professional nutrition role.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Contact Visio Nova Mundi</a>
    </div>
    <p class="safeguard"><strong>This award covers a controlled six-session pilot. It does not establish a permanent Unity House Centre, a public waste-collection service or an active food-surplus operation.</strong></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="sectionHead">
    <p class="eyebrow">What we are learning</p>
      <h2>Community insight before larger claims</h2>
      <p>With informed consent, participants may be invited to complete short feedback forms or share their views in a conversation about the pilot. We would ask only for information needed to understand opinions, access barriers and what support residents value.</p>
      <p>Responses would be handled under an agreed privacy notice and safeguarding process. Participation would be voluntary, and feedback would not determine eligibility for services or support.</p>
      <p class="note"><strong>Community insights will support evaluation of this pilot and inform feasibility work for any future Unity House centre.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="sectionHead">
    <p class="eyebrow">Beyond the funded pilot · Future Unity House Centres model</p>
      <h2>Local proof first, potential UK replication later</h2>
      <p>The pilot provides a bounded learning step, not a finished centre. The wider Unity House model is intended to be locally adaptable rather than dependent on one locality or building. A permanent neighbourhood hub or wider UK network would only be considered after credible evidence, partners, permissions and sustainable resources are in place.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flow"><div><strong>1</strong><span>One evidenced local need</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>One trusted host</span></div><div><strong>3</strong><span>One suitable resource stream</span></div><div><strong>4</strong><span>Appropriate partners</span></div><div><strong>5</strong><span>Responsible coordination</span></div><div><strong>6</strong><span>Evidence and learning</span></div></div>
    <p class="formula">1 evidenced local need + 1 trusted host + 1 suitable resource stream + appropriate partners + responsible evidence = 1 testable local Unity House node</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid section">
    <article class="card highlight vnm-glass-card"><p class="eyebrow">Pilot activity</p><h2>Community kitchen and cultural connection</h2><p>The funded pilot explores Romanian-English healthy cooking, shared learning and community connection with people from Romanian, British, Polish and other local communities. Any future surplus-food, collection or processing activity would require an appropriate host, food-safety controls and council or other required approvals.</p></article>
    <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><p class="eyebrow">Future community exchange</p><h2>Bringing people together safely</h2><p>Subject to consent, safeguarding and partner approval, future activities could include hosted cultural visits, intergenerational gatherings, park walks, cooking sessions and companionship for older people who feel isolated. No home visits or exchanges would take place without formal risk assessment and clear participant protections.</p></article>
  </section>

  <section class="section boundary">
    <div class="sectionHead"><p class="eyebrow">Responsible development</p><h2>Clear scope for this pilot and future centres</h2><p>The funded sessions follow the agreed grant scope and the Council and venue requirements. A permanent centre or additional collection, food-handling or waste-treatment activity would need its own partners, resources, permissions and readiness checks.</p><p class="note"><strong>Unity House is designed to connect with and learn from community organisations already working locally.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="cards four"><article class="smallCard vnm-glass-card"><h3>No permanent centre yet</h3><p>The award funds six sessions, not a finished Unity House building or UK-wide network.</p></article><article class="smallCard vnm-glass-card"><h3>No automatic waste handling</h3><p>Future resource streams would need separate partners, permissions and lawful treatment routes.</p></article><article class="smallCard vnm-glass-card"><h3>No clinical service</h3><p>The pilot provides health promotion and signposting, not diagnosis, treatment or clinical advice.</p></article><article class="smallCard vnm-glass-card"><h3>No invented outcomes</h3><p>Learning and participant feedback will be reported within the pilot's evidence and consent boundaries.</p></article></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section supportBar vnm-glass-card"><div><h2>Would you like to get involved?</h2><p>We are looking for careful conversations with residents, volunteers, community connectors and potential hosts who can help us understand local needs responsibly.</p></div><a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Contact Visio Nova Mundi</a></section>

  <style>
    .heroBlock{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.25fr .75fr;gap:18px;align-items:start}.eyebrow{margin:0 0 9px;color:#0f766e;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;font-size:12px;font-weight:850}h1{margin:0 0 12px;font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,64px);letter-spacing:-.04em;color:var(--text)}.lead{margin:0;max-width:72ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;font-size:19px}.actions{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:18px}.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border-radius:14px;padding:11px 14px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:white;color:var(--text);text-decoration:none;font-weight:850}.btn.primary{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.10),rgba(16,185,129,.10));border-color:rgba(39,99,235,.25)}.btn:hover{border-color:rgba(0,0,0,.18);text-decoration:none}.statusCard,.card,.smallCard,.supportBar{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:18px;background:white;box-shadow:0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.05)}.statusCard{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.07),rgba(16,185,129,.07))}.statusCard.vnm-glass-card,.card.vnm-glass-card,.smallCard.vnm-glass-card,.supportBar.vnm-glass-card{border-color:rgba(37,99,235,.2);background-image:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(37,99,235,.12),rgba(16,185,129,.10));background-color:var(--glass);box-shadow:0 10px 40px rgba(37,99,235,.12),inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.64);-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(20px) saturate(130%);backdrop-filter:blur(20px) saturate(130%);color:var(--text)}.statusCard.vnm-glass-card h2,.card.vnm-glass-card h2,.smallCard.vnm-glass-card h3,.supportBar.vnm-glass-card h2{color:var(--text)}.statusCard.vnm-glass-card p,.card.vnm-glass-card p,.smallCard.vnm-glass-card p,.supportBar.vnm-glass-card p{color:var(--muted)}.statusLabel{margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;font-size:12px;font-weight:850}.statusCard h2,.card h2,.supportBar h2{margin:0 0 9px;color:var(--text);font-size:21px;letter-spacing:-.02em}.statusCard p,.card p,.smallCard p,.supportBar p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.statusPill{display:inline-block;margin-top:14px;padding:7px 10px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.28);color:#0f766e;font-size:12px;font-weight:850;background:rgba(16,185,129,.08)}.section{margin-top:34px}.sectionHead h2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:29px;letter-spacing:-.025em;color:var(--text)}.sectionHead>p:not(.eyebrow){margin:0;max-width:90ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75}.sectionHead>.note{margin-top:12px!important;font-size:13px}.modelIntro{padding:22px;border:1px solid rgba(37,99,235,.2);border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(37,99,235,.08),rgba(16,185,129,.08))}.modelIntro .sectionHead>p:not(.eyebrow)+p{margin-top:12px}.modelGrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:16px}.modelGrid .card{padding:15px}.modelGrid .card h3{margin:0 0 7px;color:var(--text);font-size:16px}.modelGrid .card p{font-size:14px}.communityUpdate{padding:22px;border:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.24);border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(16,185,129,.08),rgba(39,99,235,.06))}.communityUpdate h2{margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--text);font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.025em}.communityUpdate>p:not(.eyebrow):not(.safeguard){color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75}.volunteerRow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;margin-top:18px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.2)}.volunteerBoundary{margin:0;max-width:72ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.safeguard{margin:18px 0 0;padding:13px 15px;border-left:3px solid #d97706;background:rgba(245,158,11,.09);color:var(--text)!important;line-height:1.7}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;align-items:start}.highlight{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.06),rgba(16,185,129,.06))}.note{margin-top:12px!important;font-size:13px}.flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px;margin-top:16px}.flow div{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:13px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:rgba(39,99,235,.04);color:var(--text);font-weight:750}.flow strong{display:grid;place-items:center;flex:0 0 28px;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(39,99,235,.12);color:#1d4ed8}.formula{margin:14px 0 0;padding:13px 15px;border:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.18);border-radius:14px;background:rgba(16,185,129,.06);color:var(--text);line-height:1.6;font-weight:750}.boundary{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:25px}.cards.four{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:14px}.smallCard{padding:14px}.smallCard h3{margin:0 0 7px;color:var(--text);font-size:16px}.smallCard p{font-size:14px}.supportBar{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.06),rgba(16,185,129,.06))}.supportBar>div{max-width:75ch}.controlNote{margin:18px 0 0;padding:13px 15px;border-left:3px solid #d97706;background:rgba(245,158,11,.09);color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;font-size:13px}@media(max-width:1100px){.flow,.modelGrid{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:900px){.heroBlock,.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.flow,.cards.four,.modelGrid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.supportBar,.volunteerRow{flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch}}@media(max-width:520px){.flow,.cards.four,.modelGrid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.communityUpdate{padding:18px}.supportBar{padding:16px}.btn{width:100%}}
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
